# THIS TEMPLATE'S BYTES ARE WHAT `wip init` COPIES, AND WHAT `lanes-edit.sh`
# EDITS ONE LINE AT A TIME.
#
# `templates/workspace-root/` ships no `contracts/` and no digest pin —
# lane-collision-protocol Amendment 9 clause (d) gives it no scripts, no
# manifest, no CI, so there is nothing here for `scripts/validate-pins.py`
# to check the way it checks `assembly-root` and `family-root`. But
# `openRepoTools wip init` still copies this template byte for byte into a
# fresh `<user>-wip` repository, the same way `scaffold-project.py` copies
# `assembly-root` into a new project, and the register it seeds,
# `lanes/LANES.md`, is then read and written a WHOLE LINE at a time by the
# installed `lanes-edit.sh` (`append-row-status`, `replace-in-row`, and the
# rest — see this template's own `AGENTS.md`, rule 1). Git for Windows'
# installer default is `core.autocrlf=true`; a materialized workspace
# checked out under it turns every `\n` here into `\r\n`, and a line-based
# edit that expects to match or move exactly one line goes blind or wrong on
# a file nobody told the owner was different — the same failure this
# repository's OWN root `.gitattributes` (#63) exists to prevent for a clone
# of openRepoShape itself.
#
# NO PATH IS LISTED BY NAME, for the same reason the other templates name
# none: every file this template ships is text, so there is nothing for
# git's binary heuristic to misjudge.
#
# openRepoShape #154 (Amendment 9 clause (d), the `templates/workspace-root/`
# template); the pattern this rule follows: `templates/assembly-root/` and
# `templates/family-root/`'s own copies, openRepoShape #51 (2026-09-05).

* text=auto eol=lf
